Database migrations (Alembic). Run these from the backend/ folder with the venv active.

The app applies pending migrations automatically when it starts.

After changing app/db/models.py, create a migration and review it before committing:
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
    alembic upgrade head

Other useful commands:
    alembic current          # which revision the database is at
    alembic history          # all revisions
    alembic downgrade -1     # undo the last migration

The database URL comes from DATABASE_URL in .env (not alembic.ini).
SQLite uses batch mode, because it can't ALTER most columns in place.
